# Summary
Introduced bug: the patch added required persisted source-route fields for metadata-transfer markers but missed preserving them in the existing set_pg_acting_set Peering path. That path can now write internally inconsistent state which the same code refuses to parse.
The new version-11 control-plane state format requires a Peering PG with a metadata transfer marker to also have both peering_metadata_transfer_source_route_epoch and peering_metadata_transfer_source_node_id. set_pg_acting_set_with_metadata_transfer correctly populates those fields. However, the regular set_pg_acting_set path can operate on a PG that is already Peering with peering_metadata_transfer set, preserves that transfer marker, and then explicitly clears the new source-route fields. format_pg_record will serialize the transfer marker with '-' for the new source fields, while parse_pg_record rejects version-11 records where a transfer marker is present but either source-route field is missing. This can make the control-plane state file unopenable after restart following an acting-set change during an in-progress metadata transfer, causing persistent availability impact until manual state repair.

# Resolution
Fixed by commit https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/7d4951c7 (`7d4951c7 Preserve metadata transfer source route fields`).

The fix keeps the metadata-transfer marker and its source-route provenance fields as a single invariant in the ordinary `set_pg_acting_set` Peering path. When an in-progress Peering metadata transfer is preserved across an acting-set update, `peering_metadata_transfer_source_route_epoch` and `peering_metadata_transfer_source_node_id` are now preserved with `peering_metadata_transfer` instead of being cleared. If there is no transfer marker, the source-route fields remain absent.

The commit also adds `peering_acting_set_update_preserves_metadata_transfer_source_route_fields`, which installs a metadata-transfer marker, performs an ordinary Peering acting-set update, reloads the persisted control-plane state, and verifies that the transfer marker and complete source-route fields survived the update.

Verified with:
- `cargo test -p storage peering_acting_set_update_preserves_metadata_transfer_source_route_fields -- --nocapture`
- `cargo test -p storage control_plane -- --nocapture`
- `cargo clippy -p storage --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `git diff --check`

