## Report
Validated the finding dynamically against commit 79babf8d115352ee7295831d70ac5956cd7ca644. Code inspection confirmed the invariant mismatch: crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:1777-1804 preserves an existing peering_metadata_transfer marker in set_pg_acting_set but clears peering_metadata_transfer_source_route_epoch and peering_metadata_transfer_source_node_id at lines 1803-1804. The dedicated transfer path sets all three fields together at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:1907-1910. Serialization at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:4360-4377 writes the transfer proof plus the source-route fields, using '-' for None, and parsing rejects version-11 records with a transfer marker but incomplete source-route fields at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:5263-5271.

I added a bounded PoC example at crates/storage/examples/metadata_transfer_route_poc.rs. It creates an Active PG on node 1, installs a metadata-transfer marker while moving it to node 2, sends a valid Peering observation from node 2, then calls the ordinary set_pg_acting_set to expand the acting set to [2,3]. The PoC lines 103-115 verify set_pg_acting_set_with_metadata_transfer initially populated the source-route fields; lines 119-127 exercise the regular acting-set path; lines 129-145 show the marker is preserved, source-route fields are None, and restart fails/panics when unwrapped.

Non-panic reproduction command output: `cargo run -p storage --example metadata_transfer_route_poc` printed `transfer marker preserved: Some(...)`, `source-route fields after regular acting-set change: epoch=None, node=None`, `serialized current PG line: pg=42,peering,2:3,-,-,-,-,9,110,11,9,9,10,11,9,110,11,-,-,0,0,-,0`, and `restart parse error: control-plane state parse error at line 44: metadata transfer source route fields require a complete transfer marker`.

Crash-style reproduction command output: `RUST_BACKTRACE=1 cargo run -p storage --example metadata_transfer_route_poc -- --panic-on-restart` exited 101 and panicked at `crates/storage/examples/metadata_transfer_route_poc.rs:145:17` with `called Result::unwrap() on an Err value: Parse { line: 44, message: "metadata transfer source route fields require a complete transfer marker" }`. This demonstrates that the code can persist a state file that the same control-plane startup path refuses to parse. Valgrind was attempted but is not installed in the container. A debugger attempt using lldb stopped at the unwrap immediately after the bad state was written and showed frame #0 at metadata_transfer_route_poc.rs:145.

